Note that VAX software follows a convention of treating registers r0 and r1 as temporaries that are not saved across a procedure call, so the VMS C compiler does include registers r0 and r1 in the register saving mask. Also, the C compiler should have used r1 instead of 8(ap) in the add13 instruction; such examples inspire computer architects to try to write compilers!

